    {
      "index": 4,
      "id": "contribution",
      "heading": "Contribution",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s04_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s04_c1_crop_makes_three_main_contributions",
          "text": "CROP makes three main contributions. First, it defines two certification criteria for reinforcement learning: robustness of the per-state action, and a lower bound on the cumulative reward.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "crop",
            "makes",
            "three",
            "main",
            "contributions",
            "first",
            "defines",
            "two",
            "certification",
            "criteria"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s04_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s04_c2_second_turns_criterion_algorithm_cro",
          "text": "Second, it turns each criterion into an algorithm. CROP-LoAct uses local randomized smoothing to certify a radius around each state within which the chosen action cannot change.",
          "expected_role": "result",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "second",
            "turns",
            "criterion",
            "algorithm",
            "crop-loact",
