    {
      "index": 5,
      "id": "method",
      "heading": "Method",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c1_engine_crop_functional_smoothing_sta",
          "text": "The engine of CROP is functional smoothing. At each state, and for each action, the method adds Gaussian noise to the state and averages the trained Q-network's output, producing a smoothed value function.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "engine",
            "crop",
            "functional",
            "smoothing",
            "state",
            "action",
            "method",
            "adds",
            "gaussian",
            "noise"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c2_key_lemma_shows_smoothed_function",
          "text": "A key lemma shows this smoothed function is Lipschitz continuous, with a constant that shrinks as the smoothing variance grows. From that continuity, Theorem 1 gives a certified radius: as long as the perturbation is smaller than this radius, the smoothed policy's action does not change.",
          "expected_role": "guidance",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "key",
            "lemma",
            "shows",
            "smoothed",
            "function",
            "lipschitz",
            "continuous",
            "constant",
            "shrinks",
            "smoothing"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c3_radius_depends_gap_between_best",
          "text": "The radius depends on the gap between the best and runner-up smoothed action-values, revealing a trade-off, since more smoothing stabilizes the values but also narrows their margin.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "radius",
            "depends",
            "gap",
            "between",
            "best",
            "runner-up",
            "smoothed",
            "action-values",
            "revealing",
            "trade-off"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c4_cumulative_reward_global_smoothing_t",
          "text": "For cumulative reward, global smoothing treats the whole trajectory as a function to bound the expected and percentile reward, while the adaptive local search of CROP-LoRe grows a trajectory tree to certify a tight absolute lower bound.",
          "expected_role": "figure",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "cumulative",
            "reward",
            "global",
            "smoothing",
            "treats",
            "whole",
